{
  "title": "Taweez against Bewitchment",
  "data": "For a man who has been bewitched so that he cannot approach his wife, write on a sheet of paper the first two verses of [Surah al-Fath](A52), [Surah al-Nasr](A114), and the following holy verses and words:\nوَمِنْ اٰيَاتِهٖ اَنْ خَلَقَ لَكُمْ مِنْ اَنْفُسِكُمْ اَزْوَاجًا لِتَسْكُنُوْا اِلَيْهَا وَجَعَلَ بَيْنَكُمْ مَوَدَّةً وَرَحْمَةً اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَاٰيَاتٍ لِقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ\nWA MIN AAYAATIHEE AN KHALAQA LAKUM MIN ANFUSIKUM AZWAAJAN LITASKUNOO ILAYHAA WA JA'ALA BAYNAKUM MAWADDATAN WA RAHMATAN INNA FEE DHAALIKA LI-AAYAATIN LIQAWMIN YATAFAKKAROON\nAnd one of His signs is that He created mates for you from yourselves that you may find rest in them, and He put between you love and compassion; most surely there are signs in this for a people who reflect. (30:21)\nثُمَّ ادْخُلُوْا عَلَيْهِمُ الْبَابَ فَاِذَا دَخَلْتُمُوْهُ فَاِنَّكُمْ غَالِبُوْنَ\nTHUMMAD KHULOO A'LAYHIMUL BAABA FA-IDHAA DAKHALTUMOOHU FA-INNAKUM GHAALIBOON\nThen enter upon them by the gate, for when you have entered it you shall surely be victorious. (5:23)\nفَفَتَحْنَا اَبْوَابَ السَّمَاۤءِ بِمَاۤءٍ مُنْهَمِرٍ وَفَجَّرْنَا الْاَرْضَ عُيُوْنًا فَالْتَقَى الْمَاۤءُ عَلٰى اَمْرٍ قَدْ قُدِرَ\nFAFATAHNAA ABWAABAS SAMAA'I BIMAA'IN MUNHAMIRIN WA FAJJARNAL ARDA U'YOONAN FALTAQAL MAA'U A'LAA AMRIN QAD QUDIR\nSo We opened the gates of the heaven with water pouring down, and We made the earth gush forth with springs, so the water gathered together according to a measure already ordained. (54:11-12)\nرَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِىْ صَدْرِىْ وَيَسِّرْ لِىْ اَمْرِىْ وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِّنْ لِّسَانِىْ يَفْقَهُوْا قَوْلِىْ\nRABBISH RAH LEE SADREE WA YASSIR LEE AMREE WAHLUL U'QDATAM MIL LISAANEE YAFQAHOO QAWLEE\nMy Lord! Expand my breast for me, make my affair easy for me, and loosen the knot from my tongue, (that) they may understand my word. (20:25-28)\nوَتَرَكْنَا بَعْضَهُمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ يَّمُوْجُ فِىْ بَعْضٍ وَنُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ فَجَمَعْنَاهُمْ جَمْعًا\nWA TARAKNAA BA'DAHUM YAWMA'IDHIN YAMOOJU FEE BA'DIN WA NUFIKHA FIS SOORI FAJAMA'NAAHUM JAM'AA\nAnd on that day We will leave a part of them in conflict with another, and the trumpet will be blown, so We will gather them all together. (18:99)\nكَذٰلِكَ حَلَلْتُ فُلَانَ بْنَ فُلَانٍ عَنْ بِنْتِ فُلَانَةَ\nKADHAALIKA HALALTU FULAANABNA FULAANIN A'N BINTI FULAANAH\nIn this way I have untied so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, from the daughter of so-and-so.\nلَقَدْ جَاۤئَكُمْ رَسُوْلٌ مِّنْ اَنْفُسِكُمْ عَزِيْزٌ عَلَيْهِ مَا عَنِتُّمْ حَرِيْصٌ عَلَيْكُمْ بِالْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ رَؤُفٌ رَّحِيْمٌ\nLAQAD JAA'AKUM RASOOLUM MIN ANFUSIKUM A'ZEEZUN A'LAYHI MAA A'NITTUM HAREESUN A'LAYKUM BIL MU'MINEENA RA'UFUR RAHEEM\nCertainly a Messenger has come to you from among yourselves; grievous to him is your falling into distress, excessively solicitous respecting you; to the believers (he is) compassionate, merciful. (9:128)\nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَقُلْ حَسْبِىَ اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ وَهُوَ رَبُّ الْعَرْشِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nFA-IN TAWALLAW FAQUL HASBIYALLAAHU LAA ILAAHA ILLAA HUWA A'LAYHI TAWAKKALTU WA HUWA RABBUL A'RSHIL A'ZEEM\nBut if they turn back, say: Allah is sufficient for me; there is no god but He; on Him do I rely, and He is the Lord of the mighty Throne. (9:129)\nThe man should keep this amulet with him and hang it above his bed. In place of “so-and-so, the son of so-and-so”, mention the man's name and his father's name, and in place of “the daughter of so-and-so”, the woman's name and her mother's name."
